Z||000000||Pike||10-08-2001||01:12 AM||||What is the story on the front heat shield. The one closest to the cabin side of the engine. when I rebuilt my 2.8 I left the sucker off. It's the one that bolts between the exhaust manifold and the block. I've hear something about a recall?<BR>thanks,<BR>Pike||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-08-2001||03:05 PM||||The heat shield installed between the head and the manifold, was part of a recall package 88-C-24...  "To reduce the effects of fluid leaks which may lead to engine compartment fires..."    <P>The description of the part is "Deflector asm - vlv rkr cvr oil (LH)," which suggests to me that it's supposed to keep oil (leaking from the valve cover) from getting on something else... the catalytic converter, I would guess.  ||||reg||1
